<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="030" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Job B propose — Action proposes allow-listed field updates (reads `sprk_emailupdatefield`), old→new, cited source + confidence, stored as pending (NOT applied)</title>
    <phase>P3 — Job B record currency</phase>
    <gate>after:020,022,001</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <tags>bff-api, catalog, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Record-currency proposal generation on the correctness-critical Job B path. Reads the `sprk_emailupdatefield` allow-list and produces field-update proposals that a human will later confirm and apply (031). The allow-list gate + citation + verify-cited-text + confidence obligations (NFR-06 / ADR-015) are load-bearing trust properties — a non-allow-listed field proposed, or a citation that does not exist in the source, is a defect. BFF-touching (Services/Communication + Services/Ai via PublicContracts): publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification required; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Trust-critical proposal generation with an allow-list gate, citation verification, and confidence scoring on a record-mutating path; reasoning quality on "propose only what is enabled + cited + real" is the exact failure mode that erodes trust if reasoned sloppily.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares the Job B proposal surface + `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams with 031/032; never run concurrently with other shared `Services/Communication/` writers. `/conflict-check` before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>020, 022, 001</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement **Job B — propose** (FR-09): the triage/action path proposes **allow-listed** field updates on the record the email is associated to (from the 7-entity identifier rung, 020), each proposal carrying **old value → new value, the cited source text (email body or attachment + locator), and a confidence score**, stored as a **pending proposal** — NOT applied. Application is a separate, human-confirmed step (031).

    The allow-list is authoritative and read-only to r1: read `sprk_emailupdatefield` (created + seeded by the operator; verified in 001). Job B may propose an update to a `(sprk_targetentity, sprk_targetfield)` pair **ONLY** when there is an **enabled** row for it (`sprk_enabled = true`). A field with no enabled row is **never** proposed — no exceptions, no arbitrary column writes. Honor the per-row coercion hint (`sprk_fieldtype`) and extraction guidance (`sprk_extractionguidance`); `sprk_requireconfirm` is true in P1 (every proposal requires human confirm at 031).

    Reach AI **only** through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` (ADR-013 facade) and produce the proposal via a **code-directed Action + Binding** (ADR-039). MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph playbook engine (`PlaybookOrchestrationService` / `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor` / `IInvokePlaybookAi` — deleted). Reuse the classification signal already produced on the enrichment path (022) — do not run a second full LLM pass where the triage/classification output already exists.

    **Trust invariants (NFR-06 / ADR-015):** every proposal carries a plain-language reason + a citation to exact source text, and the system **verifies the cited text actually exists** in the source communication/attachment before storing the proposal (a proposal whose cited text cannot be located is dropped, not stored). Nothing deadline-bearing / privilege-adjacent auto-finalizes; privilege is flagged, never decided. **NFR-04:** proposal generation MUST be best-effort / non-fatal — it MUST NOT fail the capture or send path.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication + Ai domains. Authority on the Job B proposal path, the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade (ADR-013), Action + Binding authoring (ADR-039), the `sprk_emailupdatefield` allow-list contract (C-4 / FR-11), and the NFR-06 / ADR-015 trust-and-audit obligations. Fluent in the r5 feed/apply coordination contract (`notes/email-intelligence-r1-coordination.md`).
  </role>

  <goal>
    Given an email associated to a record (020) with triage output already produced (022), Job B generates zero-or-more **pending** field-update proposals — each with old→new value, a verified citation (source + locator), a plain-language reason, and a confidence — restricted to `(entity, field)` pairs that have an **enabled** row in `sprk_emailupdatefield`. Proposals are stored (not applied) in a shape the 031 apply endpoint and the 032 queue-feed can consume and r5 can render. A non-allow-listed / disabled field is never proposed. A proposal whose cited text cannot be located in the source is never stored. Proposal generation is non-fatal to capture/send. Build clean; unit + seam tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      r1 makes matched records **current from email**. Job B is FULL depth (propose → confirm → apply → audit; owner-locked). This task is the **propose** half: it reads the operator-owned allow-list and emits pending proposals; 031 applies a confirmed one under OBO and writes the audit row; 032 exposes the ranked exceptions feed r5 renders. r1 builds no UI — the confirm/apply card is r5's (C-3); r1 supplies the stored proposals + apply endpoint (coordination doc).

      The allow-list (`sprk_emailupdatefield`, C-4 / FR-11) is the safety boundary: `sprk_targetentity` → `sprk_recordtype_ref`, `sprk_targetfield`, `sprk_enabled`, `sprk_fieldtype` (coercion hint), `sprk_requireconfirm` (=true in P1), `sprk_extractionguidance`. Without it, Job B could propose arbitrary column writes — unsafe. r1 reads it defensively; it is operator-created (verified in 001).

      Reuse-first: the classification/triage signal from 022 already exists on the enrichment path — Job B grounds proposals in it and in the associated record's current field values (old→new needs the current value). No second full LLM pass.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (REUSE — the write-core facade seam; Job B propose consumes the Action path here, not internals)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/UpdateRecordActionCore.cs (REFERENCE — the update-record write core the propose shape targets; 031 invokes it, 030 shapes the proposal for it)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ICommunicationClassificationAi.cs (REUSE — classification facade; reuse the existing signal, no 2nd full LLM pass)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/AiClassificationRung.cs (REFERENCE — the classification substrate produced on the enrichment path, 022)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs (REFERENCE — enrichment path where triage output is produced; propose runs best-effort here, NFR-04)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (REFERENCE — the endpoint family 031/032 extend; 030 stores proposals these read)</file>
      <file>sprk_emailupdatefield (Dataverse — operator-owned allow-list; READ-ONLY to r1; verified in 001; governs what may be proposed)</file>
      <file>sprk_emailreviewlog (Dataverse — append-only audit; 031 writes the human-decision row; 030's proposal is the "AI proposed" source of that row)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json (REFERENCE — Binding row shape for the propose Action)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md (Action + Binding authoring; PublicContracts facade path)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/email-intelligence-r1-coordination.md (r5 feed/apply contract — the stored-proposal shape r5 renders)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>020 (the association that supplies the target record), 022 (the triage/classification signal to reuse), 001 (verifies `sprk_emailupdatefield` exists + seeded).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-09">Scope: propose allow-listed field updates on the associated record; each proposal carries old→new value, cited source text (email/attachment + locator), a plain-language reason, and confidence; stored as PENDING (not applied). A non-allow-listed / disabled field is NEVER proposed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-11 / C-4">Scope: the `sprk_emailupdatefield` allow-list is authoritative + READ-ONLY to r1; propose ONLY for `(sprk_targetentity, sprk_targetfield)` pairs with `sprk_enabled = true`; honor `sprk_fieldtype` coercion + `sprk_extractionguidance`; `sprk_requireconfirm` is true in P1. Do NOT create/modify the table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-015">Scope: every proposal carries a plain-language reason + citation to exact source text; the system MUST verify the cited text exists in the source before storing (drop, do not store, if unlocatable). Nothing deadline-bearing / privilege-adjacent auto-finalizes; privilege is flagged, never decided.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: proposal generation is a code-directed Action + Binding via catalog data; MUST NOT land capability on the frozen node-graph engine (`PlaybookOrchestrationService` / `UpdateRecordNodeExecutor` / `IInvokePlaybookAi` — deleted).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-03">Scope: reach AI ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient` / `IPlaybookService` into Communication code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04 / ADR-045">Scope: proposal generation is best-effort / non-fatal — it MUST NOT fail the capture or send path; a proposal failure logs + degrades, never throws up the enrichment path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` before designing; state Placement Justification in the PR (extends the Communication + Ai domains, reuses the PublicContracts facade, no new top-level service); report publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl. PDBs; expected ≈0, no new heavy dep); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + seam tests (ADR-038).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §11">Scope: Component Justification — the pending-proposal store is new only because there is no existing per-email proposal record; state the concrete FR-09 failure mode prevented (Job B could write arbitrary columns) with grep evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07 / ADR-039">Scope: the propose Action/Binding adds a golden-utterance eval case (blocking merge gate).</constraint>
  </constraints>

