    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Allow-list-gated proposal" location="sprk_emailupdatefield (Dataverse)">
        Read the enabled rows for the associated entity; propose ONLY `(entity, field)` pairs present + enabled; coerce per `sprk_fieldtype`; ground extraction in `sprk_extractionguidance`. No enabled row → no proposal.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Verify-cited-text" location="Services/Communication/">
        For each candidate proposal, locate the cited span in the source communication/attachment text; if not found, DROP the proposal (never store an unverifiable citation).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Reuse classification signal" location="Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/AiClassificationRung.cs">
        Ground the proposal in the triage/classification output already produced on the enrichment path (022) + the record's current field values (for old→new); no second full LLM pass.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (§F/§G + §11), `docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md`, ADR-039 (code-directed Action + Binding), ADR-013 (PublicContracts facade), ADR-015 (privilege flagged never decided), and the coordination doc (stored-proposal shape r5 renders).</step>
    <step order="2">Read `IActionSeam.cs`, `UpdateRecordActionCore.cs`, `ICommunicationClassificationAi.cs`, and the enrichment path — identify the facade entry point, the update-record write-core shape 031 will invoke, and where the triage/classification signal (022) is available on the enrichment path.</step>
    <step order="3">Author the propose Action + Binding (catalog data + PublicContracts) that, given the associated record + reused classification signal, emits candidate `(field, oldValue, newValue, citation{source, locator}, reason, confidence)` proposals. Grep to confirm no existing per-email proposal store exists (§11 evidence).</step>
    <step order="4">Read `sprk_emailupdatefield` defensively; filter candidates to `(sprk_targetentity, sprk_targetfield)` pairs with `sprk_enabled = true`; apply `sprk_fieldtype` coercion + `sprk_extractionguidance`. Drop any candidate for a non-listed/disabled field.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify-cited-text: for each surviving candidate, confirm the cited span exists in the source communication/attachment; DROP any whose citation cannot be located (NFR-06). Attach the plain-language reason + confidence.</step>
    <step order="6">Store surviving proposals as PENDING (not applied), in the shape the 031 apply endpoint + 032 queue-feed + r5 consume (per coordination doc). Run the whole propose step best-effort on the enrichment path (NFR-04) — log + degrade on failure, never throw up capture/send.</step>
    <step order="7">Add the golden-utterance eval case (NFR-07) for the propose Action/Binding. Write unit + seam tests: (a) an enabled allow-list field with a cited fact yields a pending proposal (old→new + citation + confidence); (b) NEGATIVE — a non-allow-listed / disabled field is NEVER proposed; (c) NEGATIVE — a candidate whose cited text is absent from the source is NOT stored; (d) proposal generation failure does not fail the enrichment path (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; run the BFF publish-size check (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `code-review` (focus allow-list gate, verify-cited-text, no frozen-engine landing, facade discipline, non-fatal); `adr-check` against ADR-039 / ADR-013 / ADR-015 + spec FR-09 / FR-11 / NFR-04 / NFR-06 / NFR-07. Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (030 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (proposal store shape, allow-list read point, verify-cited-text approach) for 031/032.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If reusing the classification signal (022) proves insufficient to produce a defensible old→new proposal without a second full LLM pass — or if the allow-list contract (`sprk_emailupdatefield`) as verified in 001 cannot express a required coercion/guidance the propose path needs — STOP and surface per root §6 / §6.5 rather than adding a second LLM pass or writing to the operator-owned table.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing per-email field-update proposal record; `sprk_emailreviewlog` (012) is the append-only audit, not a pending-proposal store; the Field Mapping Framework is creation-time value copy (different intent).</existing>
    <extension>No — the audit log records decisions after the fact and cannot hold a pending, human-confirmable proposal with citation + confidence; the propose surface is a new stored shape produced by a code-directed Action, reusing the PublicContracts facade + the update-record write core (not forked).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the allow-list-gated pending-proposal store, Job B could either propose arbitrary column writes (unsafe) or have nothing for r5 to render + 031 to apply — FR-09 fails and the record-currency pillar (G-5 / Success Criterion 6) does not ship.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect the facade seam, update-record core, classification facade, enrichment path, endpoints, allow-list contract, coordination doc</tool>
    <tool name="grep">Confirm no existing per-email proposal store (§11 evidence); confirm no `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` injected into Communication code</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Author the propose Action/Binding + proposal store + enrichment-path wiring</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Build, unit/seam tests, publish-size, CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Pre-PR hot-path scan (Step 10)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ + Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ (UPDATED — Job B propose path: allow-list-gated, cited, confidence-scored pending proposals via a code-directed Action, best-effort on enrichment)</output>
    <output type="config">infra/dataverse/ (Action + Binding catalog rows for the propose Action + input/output schema)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/ — enabled-field proposal + non-allow-listed-never-proposed + unverifiable-citation-not-stored + non-fatal negatives; golden-utterance eval case</output>
    <output type="docs">PR description with §11 Component Justification + bff-extensions Placement Justification + publish-size delta + CVE result</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an email associated to a record with an enabled `sprk_emailupdatefield` row and a cited fact ("closing moved to Aug 15"), Job B stores a PENDING proposal for that field with old→new value, citation (source + locator), a plain-language reason, and confidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a field with no enabled `sprk_emailupdatefield` row is NEVER proposed (allow-list is the sole gate).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a candidate proposal whose cited text cannot be located in the source communication/attachment is NOT stored (verify-cited-text, NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Proposals are stored PENDING (not applied); nothing is written to the target record by this task (application is 031).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Proposal generation is best-effort: a proposal failure does NOT fail the capture or send / enrichment path (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AI is reached only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; no `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` injected; no capability landed on the frozen node-graph engine (grep-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A golden-utterance eval case exists for the propose Action/Binding (NFR-07).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; tests pass; publish-size delta ≈0 vs ~49.63 MB reported; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Blocks 031 (apply consumes the stored proposal) + 032 (queue-feed ranks stored proposals). r1 builds no UI — the confirm/apply card is r5's; r1 supplies the stored-proposal shape (coordination doc). The allow-list is operator-owned and READ-ONLY to r1. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/`).
  </notes>

